          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As they came near the village to which they were going, Jesus acted as if he were going farther; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but they held him back, saying, “Stay with us; the day is almost over and it is getting dark.” So he went in to stay with them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He sat down to eat with them, took the bread, and said the blessing; then he broke the bread and gave it to them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then their eyes were opened and they recognized him, but he disappeared from their sight. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "LUK 24:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They said to each other, “Wasn't it like a fire burning in us when he talked to us on the road and explained the Scriptures to us?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "LUK.24.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "LUK.24.32"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
